zebkit, Windows: wheel events that carry exact distances

A wheel event on the GLib ports and on macOS can say that its distances
are exact (a touchpad's, or a scroll a program asked for), and the page
then scrolls by them at once. Scrolls by the notches of a wheel are
animated when smooth scrolling is on. This port's events could not say
so: the fields are compiled for the other ports only, and every wheel
event was a notched one. They are compiled for Windows too.

And where there is no kinetic scrolling, as on Windows, an event with
exact distances was animated all the same: WebCore knows such an event
for one not to animate only from the phases that kinetic scrolling
gives. Without kinetic scrolling an event with exact distances is now
taken as one.

The port's own events, made from window messages, still say nothing,
and are animated as before; the CDP endpoint's say what they are, as on
Linux.

